# The build context for mandate-engine IS this package directory (docker-compose.yml sets
# context: ./packages/mandateEngine), so this file is live -- unlike the package-level
# .dockerignore files of the services that build from the repository root.
#
# Patterns anchor at the context root: nested matches need a leading **/ . The previous bare
# "__pycache__" matched only the top-level directory and shipped 36 .pyc files across seven
# nested __pycache__ directories into the image.

# Secrets: the Dockerfile does COPY . into the image, so an env file here would be baked in.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Python bytecode & tool caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.eggs

# Tests & coverage
**/test
**/tests
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/coverage.xml

# Docker, VCS, logs and OS noise
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/Desktop.ini
